            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-30T15:31:28+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-30T15:31:28+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-30T06:01:28Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-30T06:01:28Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A series of troughs over SA will slowly move east ahead of a high pressure system that moves into the Bight on Friday. A cold front moving across the Southern Ocean will clip the far southeast late Thursday, with a low pressure system developing near the Victorian border on Friday. Another trough near the WA border is expected to develop on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
